From: C2000MAX maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] net: mediatek: bound queue IDs to the configured QDMA count

Adapt MediaTek b0a1258f0fd86ff40f9a4e29ef2ad4950c237f6b:
https://github.com/mediatek/mtk-openwrt-feeds/commit/b0a1258f0fd86ff40f9a4e29ef2ad4950c237f6b

Apply after MAX's 64-queue extension, not by replacing the upstream eth-26
patch. The mask describes a queue ID, not a bitmap of all queues. MAX uses
64 queues (mask 0x3f), while the other configuration uses 16 (mask 0x0f).
Keep upper mark flags out of queue selection and retain HQoS QIDs 60..63.
No queue counts, direction bits, shapers or EQoS policies are changed.

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.h
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.h
@@ -33,7 +33,7 @@
 #else
 #define MTK_QDMA_NUM_QUEUES	16
 #endif
-#define MTK_QDMA_QUEUE_MASK	GENMASK(15, 0)
+#define MTK_QDMA_QUEUE_MASK	(MTK_QDMA_NUM_QUEUES - 1)
 #define MTK_QDMA_PAGE_SIZE	2048
 #define MTK_MAX_RX_LENGTH	1536
 #define MTK_MAX_RX_LENGTH_UNIT	1024
